<urn:usf:contract:atlas-capture-observer:2> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "No live reader, arbitrary filesystem/shell/network/provider/credential access, persistent service, supervisor mutation, semantic authority, remote provider contact, accepted completion, publication or deployment is granted." <urn:usf:graph:atlas-capture-observer> .
<urn:usf:requirement:atlas-capture-resources:2> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:atlas-capture-observer> .
<urn:usf:requirement:atlas-capture-resources:2> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "For the selected extraction process and all descendants, configure one temporary cgroup with MemoryMax 536870912 bytes, CPUQuota 100 percent and a 30000 millisecond wall deadline; retain observed completion/refusal and cleanup. Refuse when required controls cannot be established. MaximumCpuQuotaPercent and maximumWallMilliseconds are distinct controls, not measured CPU time or a proof of exactly 30000 CPU milliseconds. Preserve aggregate 1500-file/64MiB-input/2MiB-output and concurrency-one bounds. The current implementation admits three named carriers; the eight-repository schema ceiling is not tested capacity. Build, test and browser job limits remain individually recorded rather than inheriting an unproved extraction bound." <urn:usf:graph:atlas-capture-observer> .
